  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The choir has identified a troublesome passage, and the conductor can briefly separate its rhythm, words, and pitches before rehearsing it again.\", \"decision\": \"How should a difficult passage be diagnosed?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe choir tries rhythm, words, and pitches separately in a short sequence before the conductor selects focused practice. Comparing the separate attempts helps reveal which element is creating trouble when everything is combined.\nThe conductor listens to the passage and chooses one element for the choir to isolate before recombining it. A single diagnosis concentrates practice time on the feature the conductor judges most responsible for the difficulty.\nSingers describe where the passage becomes uncertain, and the conductor selects an element to isolate from those reports. The practice exercise addresses experienced points of confusion as well as what can be heard from the front."
    }
  ],
